validation=f'''STRATUS 1.6.4 — VALIDATION\n20 October 2026\n\nNative macOS OpenGL: 768 compile/link pairs across eight variants, zero failures.\nIncludes defaults, vanilla sky, Fast/Balanced/Reference/High, option extremes and\nOverworld/Nether/End programs. Compatibility shims do not emulate every Iris\ntransformation. All 53 reachable controls have English labels. Shadows stay off.\n\n122 candidate GPU renders passed, zero OpenGL errors: 91 actual material-response\nsamples with 248 independent invariants/relationships; 10 full water-resolve\ncases; 3 water-raster attachment/blending cases; 18 cloud-integrator samples\nacross nine angular thresholds and three sampling budgets. Cloud opacity is\ncompared with an independent dense CPU integral through an analytic volume.\nHistorical diagnostic renders are not counted as candidate passes.\n\nActual Main / Stratus Terrain Lab (normal world, Creative) loaded the immutable\nfinal shader assets in Stratus-1.6.4-Verify-CloudRange.zip and all four preset\naliases plus vanilla sky mode. Minecraft 1.21.11 / Iris 1.10.8 / Sodium 0.8.14 /\nApple M1 OpenGL 4.1. No shader compilation failures appeared. {len(captures)} captures were\ninspected; the visual report labels baseline controls, supporting material-only\nchecks and final-source retests separately. Final-source checks cover waterline,\nsubmerged wood, upward underwater views, glass above/below water, waterfall,\nparticles, matte materials and metal, presets, cloud height/pitch changes and\nthe actual Materials settings menu. Supporting checks include biomes, enclosed\ncave lighting, sunset, night and rain. Rejected unloaded-terrain, misplaced\ncamera and experimental-cloud frames are not represented as passes.\n\nAll 235 shader/configuration/data assets in the release match the immutable\nruntime-tested archive. The test helper was project-local and session-specific,\nnever installed in Main/mods. The test client quit gracefully after saving all\ndimensions. Delivery/normal-launch status is recorded separately in the install\nreceipt and visual report, rather than inferred from this test run.\n\nPERFORMANCE: UNVERIFIED. Both diagnostic samples were unfocused. Dynamic FPS\nwas disabled only in memory during those rejected samples and then restored.\nThey establish neither normal-play FPS nor a candidate speedup. The recorded\nframebuffer was 854x480, render distance 12, simulation distance 8, cap 70,\nVSync enabled. No 60-FPS claim or hidden quality reduction.\n\nKnown limits: screen-space hidden/off-screen geometry; nearest visible water\nexit only; existing clear-sky fallback for missing exits; heuristic matte\nmoisture; bounded cloud integration while inside its layer (960 blocks at\ndefault span), with distant interior structure approximated by the background.\nNo unseen-reference exact-match or exhaustive temporal/mod compatibility claim.\n'''
(p/'VALIDATION.txt').write_text(validation);(p/'IN-GAME-TEST.txt').write_text(validation)
(p/'README.txt').write_text('''STRATUS 1.6.4 — MATTE MOISTURE AND SMOOTHER CLOUD TRAVERSAL\nOriginal Iris shader pack for Minecraft Java 1.21.11 on Apple Silicon macOS.\nTarget: GLSL 330 / OpenGL 4.1. Complete editable source and MIT license included.\n\nSolid blocks retain vanilla texture detail and matte diffuse shading. Porosity,\nface drainage, partial shelter, humidity and rain vary moisture absorption.\nThe previous sky-reflecting wet film and sun highlight are removed. Nonabsorbing\nmetal/glazed classes do not acquire porous-material absorption.\n\nMIGRATION: WET_SHEEN remains a compatible saved identifier, now labeled\nSheltered moisture retention. Its value controls extra matte absorption on\nporous partially sheltered faces. It cannot enable glossy solid-block reflections.\nExisting option values, including water extinction 3.00 and turbidity 6.00 in\nthe tested profile, were preserved. Defaults and saved overrides are distinct.\n\nClouds use continuous integration without the old power-of-two spacing jumps.\nInside the cloud volume a smooth distance bound gives nearby cloud structure\nmore useful samples instead of resolving it as distant horizontal sheets.\nThe noise field stays in world space; no temporal jitter or extra pass is added.\n\nAbove-water water optics remain. Underwater transmission stays unbent, without\na Snell window or reflection overlay. Water fog ends at the nearest visible\nexit and does not accumulate over the air beyond it. Glass and particle edges\nremain at full resolution. All presets disable cast shadows and keep solids matte.\n\nINSTALL\nPut Stratus-1.6.4.zip in the instance shaderpacks folder, keep it zipped, and\nselect it in Iris. To retain preferences, copy the previous pack's .zip.txt\noptions beside it using the new Stratus-1.6.4.zip.txt name. In Main this has\nalready been done by the delivery script; do not overwrite newer preferences.\n\nPRESETS\nFast: lowest effect resolutions, sky-only water reflections; missing terrain\nreflection is an explicit reference compromise.\nBalanced: half-resolution water/atmosphere and modest scenery tracing.\nReference: full effect resolution, detailed reflections and two cloud sample levels.\nHigh: additional cloud sampling with the same artistic direction.\nVanilla cloud and sun modes remain available independently of quality presets.\n\nVERIFICATION AND LIMITS\n768 native compile/link pairs and 122 focused candidate GPU renders passed.\nActual Main visual checks are documented in VALIDATION.txt and CHECKS.json.\nForeground FPS is unverified; no 60-FPS or speedup claim. Water screen-space\nlimits and nearest-exit behavior remain. Moisture is a visual approximation.\nInside clouds, the integration range approaches max(512, 4*CLOUD_SPAN), or 960\nblocks at default span, with distant interior structure approximated by the\nbackground. Low sampling can still soften fine detail. See validation for scope.\n''')
